  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You want to buy NNN items from a store, which you will visit on Days 111, 222, ..., NNN. The normal cost of the iii-th item is AiA_iAi​.\n\nHowever, on the iii-th day, there is a promotional event for the iii-th item. On this day, it's cost is BiB_iBi​ instead. BiB_iBi​ may be greater, smaller or even equal to AiA_iAi​.\n\nThus, on the iii-th day, the cost of the iii-th item is BiB_iBi​ while, the jjj-th item (j≠i)(j \\ne i)(j=i) costs AjA_jAj​.\n\nYou will buy **exactly one** item on each of the NNN days. All the bought items must be distinct. Find the minimum possible cost.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN - the number of items\nThe second line contains A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​ - the normal costs of the items\nThe third line contains B1,B2,....,BNB_1, B_2, ...., B_NB1​,B2​,....,BN​ - the promotional costs of the items.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum cost.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1091 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n1 2 3\n3 2 1\n2\n1 2\n2 1",
        "output": "4\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The following is a possible optimal approach :\n\nBuy Item 222 on Day 111 for cost of 222. (Normal Cost)\nBuy Item 111 on Day 222 for cost of 111. (Normal Cost)\nBuy Item 333 on Day 333 for cost of 111. (Promotional Cost)\n\nThe total cost is 2+1+1=42 + 1 + 1 = 42+1+1=4."
      }
    ]
  },
